l also has a lobby bar and the elegant eighth-story Le Melhor bar, with red silk accents, velvety red chairs, and city views. Lunches, dinners and cocktails are organised in our extraordinary private dining room on the 8th floor with a breath-taking view over Lyon.The well-being space, So FIT, offers the opportunity to discover a truly relaxing moment. With a Michelin-starred restaurant, river views, high-end service, and other amenities, this is certainly a luxury affair, but it's former five-pearl status has lost some luster over the years. Book Sofitel Lyon Bellecour, Lyon on Tripadvisor: See 2,472 traveller reviews, 887 candid photos, and great deals for Sofitel Lyon Bellecour, ranked #39 of 151 hotels in Lyon and rated 4 of 5 at Tripadvisor. <br> The crown jewel is the reservation-required Michelin-starred rated Les Trois Dômes restaurant, situated on the eighth-story, with panoramic windows that look out onto the city and Rhone. The crown jewel is the reservation-required Michelin-starred rated Les Trois Dômes restaurant, situated on the eighth-story, with panoramic windows that look out onto the city and Rhone. <br> <br>The Silk décor throughout the hotel is linked to the History of Lyon and is visible throughout your stay.The Michelin starred Chef Christian Lherm combines culinary expertise and passion in his seasonal cuisine.The Michelin starred Chef Christian Lherm combines culinary expertise and passion in his seasonal cuisine. Cour des Loges provides a boutique alternative with plush interiors.The Sofitel Lyon Bellecour is situated in a square white building that directly faces the Rhone. For more casual fare a second restaurant, The Silk Brasserie, serves up French dishes for lunch and dinner in a contemporary atmosphere. Sofitel Lyon Bellecour is an 8-story venue in the downtown district around 1350 meters from Museum of Fine Arts of Lyon and approximately 1350 meters from Basilica of Notre-Dame de Fourviere offering tasteful rooms and a high level of services. For the season, the gourmet restaurant Les Trois Forts and the brasserie Le Carré Bistromanie give way to “Le Temps d’un Eté”. A silk mural covers one wall -- a nod to Lyon's silk industry -- and makes an appearance again in the chic, red-silk ceiling bar on the eighth story. Coaches are available by appointment for a personalised session and follow up. Room service is available 24 hours.Wellness facilities include a small gym, hammam, and spa offering massages and other treatments, but there's no pool or whirlpool. The menu combines typical dishes of a brasserie such as the Club Sandwich, the Burger or the Salmon Tartar, and classics revisited like the linguini with prawns. A high-ceilinged lobby welcomes guests with dark accents, velvety purple couches, and large vases filled with flowers. Its 164 rooms invite one to discover the History of Silk of the city of Lyon. The modern equipment allow the guests to progress at their own speed. All products are independently selected by our writers and editors. For guests traveling with children, the hotel offers kids' menus, cribs, and can arrange childcare, and pets are allowed for an extra nightly fee. <br>";s:7:"keyword";s:23:"sofitel lyon restaurant";s:5:"links";s:11954:"<a href='https://backyard.synpat.com/site/article.php?page=dymatize-iso-100-prix-88a0eb'>Dymatize Iso 100 Prix</a>,
